    "sections": [
      {
        "label": "1st quarter",
        "score": "GB 14, NE 0",
        "text": "Xavier McKinney intercepted Maye's first pass and returned it to the New England 14, and two plays later Jordan Love scrambled in from 13 yards for a 7–0 lead. Love hit Matthew Golden for a 5-yard touchdown at 7:59 to make it 14–0. Green Bay lost Josh Jacobs (broken finger) and Ty'Ron Hopper (chest) in the quarter."
      },
      {
        "label": "2nd quarter",
        "score": "GB 24, NE 14",
        "text": "Trey Smack's 41-yard field goal made it 17–0 before Maye found Rhamondre Stevenson on a 30-yard touchdown. Maye threw two more interceptions in the quarter, and Kaleb Johnson's 2-yard run made it 24–7 before Efton Chism III caught an 8-yard touchdown with 2:37 left. Carlton Davis III and Ben Brown left with knee injuries."
      },
      {
        "label": "3rd quarter",
        "score": "GB 42, NE 21",
        "text": "Green Bay scored 18 straight: Love to Savion Williams for 10 yards (31–14), a 51-yard Smack field goal (34–14), then a 39-yard Love strike to Christian Watson after Isaiah McDuffie forced a Stevenson fumble, with Love running in the two-point try for 42–14. Stevenson left with a knee injury, and Maye hit Mack Hollins for a 22-yard score with 1:11 left."
      },
      {
        "label": "4th quarter",
        "score": "Final: GB 45, NE 27",
        "text": "Smack added a 38-yard field goal for 45–21, and Corey Kiner ran in from 4 yards with 3:54 left; the two-point try failed. Will Campbell left with a knee injury."
      }
    ],
